                <pb facs="0142" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg136"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>You will inform Lord Rosebery that, yielding to his desire, this Government
                    consents further negotiations for making the award of the Paris Tribunal
                    effective shall be conducted here with the British ambassador. While your
                    generous offer to visit Washington and aid us is appreciated, the President will
                    not impose the burden upon you.</p>
            </div>
